    width: 1 pixel through open bg when exits are aligned; otherwise a 2D open
      middle band/rectangle between opposite-facing but offset exits is filled by
      the all-shortest-path rule [observed in 3/4 eval examples]
    separation: blocks separated by 3-7 Manhattan distance
  output_rule: |
    Paint every bg pixel on any shortest 4-connected path between the two
    endpoints (treating wall as impassable). Additionally, fill entire NxN
    interior of any framed room that the shortest-path mask intersects.
  path_metrics:
    shortest_distance: 36-72
    turns_on_single_path: 8-21
    rooms_on_route: 6-14
    rooms_off_route: 1-8 (all off-route rooms have fully sealed walls — no doorways)
    doorway_rooms_on_route: all rooms with at least one doorway must lie on the shortest path
    middle_open_fill: optional branch where the inter-block open-space fill has
      both dimensions >1, observed bboxes 13x8, 8x6, and 8x10
    middle_open_fill_bounded: for the offset-exit branch, the middle fill bbox
      must stay within the combined span of the facing square room frames on
      both sides; it never protrudes past either side's room-frame column/row

generation_strategy:
  approach: path-first
  steps:
    - Pick two room sizes S1, S2 in 3-5 and room-grid dimensions R1xC1, R2xC2 for each block (2-14 rooms each).
    - Build block 1 as a wall-framed R1xC1 grid of S1xS1 rooms. Place one 1-pixel doorway per internal wall segment. Choose one exit doorway on the outer wall.
    - Build block 2 similarly with S2xS2 rooms and its own exit doorway.
    - Place blocks on a bg grid with 2-8 pixel gap between them, with exits facing each other.
    - In the common branch, offset the opposing exits along the perpendicular axis
      so the unobstructed middle space becomes a rectangular all-shortest-path fill
      region. Choose the offset only within the common span covered by facing
      square frames on both sides. In the minority branch, align exits and draw a
      1-pixel corridor.
    - Run BFS to verify a connected path exists from every room to every other room and through the inter-block connector.
    - Choose one room in each block for the endpoint; fill it with paint color (clip to grid boundary if at edge).
    - Verify the solver produces a non-trivial output (>=6 rooms on route, >=1 room off route).
